{
  "name": "Check every email address in a Google Sheet and write the result next to it",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Check every email address in a Google Sheet and write the result next to it\n\n### How it works\nClean a list before it costs you your sender reputation. The sheet has an email column and an empty result column. Each run reads the rows without a result, checks at most max_checks addresses with Argorant and writes the result back: valid, invalid, catch_all (the domain accepts every address), risky or unknown, plus send yes or no. Run it again to continue with the next rows.\n\nCosts: half a credit per fresh check; recent checks are free.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Create a sheet with the columns email, result, send and pick it in both Google Sheets nodes.\n4. Set max_checks in **Settings** and click Execute workflow.\n\n### Customization\nTreat catch_all as send yes if your campaigns accept them.",
        "height": 558,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "07a76018-6dd1-41b4-8552-4908eaba966a",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
